--- a/doc/liblouis.texi
+++ b/doc/liblouis.texi
@@ -2163,6 +2163,15 @@
 @emph{somewhat experimental}.
 
 @table @code
+@opcode{notallcaps, match rule}
+This modifier must immediately precede @code{match}. It skips that rule
+when every character in its matched text has the uppercase attribute.
+It allows a mixed-script table to extend ordinary word contractions
+without extending them to uppercase abbreviations. Other rules remain
+available as fallbacks. The modifier does not affect capitalization
+indicators, explicit @code{no_contract} typeforms, or unmodified tables.
+Like @code{match}, it applies only in forward translation.
+
 @opcode{match, pre-pattern characters post-pattern dots}
 
 This opcode allows for matching a string of characters via @emph{pre}
